onor_log2fc_shrunk":-3.89608e-07}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000163885","entrez_id":["348807"],"uniprot":["Q494V2"],"ncbi_summary":"Predicted to enable dynein complex binding activity. Predicted to be involved in cilium movement and inner dynein arm assembly. Located in ciliary basal body. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q494V2","text":"Microtubule-associated protein that promotes microtubule polymerization and regulates microtubule organization (PubMed:37192300). Plays a critical role in ensuring proper epidermal development and function by regulating mitosis in keratinocytes (PubMed:40593606). Maintains spindle pole integrity during keratinocyte division through the recruitment of the microtubule glutamylase TTLL13 to spindle poles, thereby enhancing localized microtubule glutamylation (PubMed:40593606). This modification stabilizes spindle microtubules, ensuring accurate spindle assembly, faithful chromosome segregation, and efficient mitotic progression (PubMed:40593606). May play a role in ciliary/flagellar motility by regulating the assembly and the activity of axonemal inner dynein arm."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}